@image{../../text/original/figures/chap3/Fig3.4b,,132mm,Figure 3.4: Procedure objects in the global frame.,.std.svg}
@end ifhtml
@iftex
@image{../../text/original/figures/pdf/chap3/Fig3.4b.std,147mm,,,.pdf}

@end iftex
@caption{@strong{Figure 3.4:} Procedure objects in the global frame.}
@end float
@noindent
In @ref{Figure 3.5} we see the environment structure created by evaluating the
expression @code{f(5)}.  The call to @code{f} creates a new environment E1
beginning with a frame in which @code{a}, the formal parameter of @code{f}, is
bound to the argument 5.  In E1, we evaluate the body of @code{f}:

@example typescript
sumOfSquares(a + 1, a * 2)
@end example

@float
@anchor{Figure 3.5}
@ifinfo
@strong{Figure 3.5:} Environments created by evaluating
@code{f(5)} using the procedures in @ref{Figure 3.4}.

@example
